    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "I do not know either, I thought you coded the getRefinements util for the current refined values widget that's why I though you knew more maybe?\n\nSince it's currently only exposed through the \"name\" attribute in the current refined value template, I would go for a string since it is stringified by default.\n\nYou could pass a transformData and expect name to be a number but I think most of the cases this is not what you want. Even if people want the original value we can add it later on in a \"value\" prop\n",
